PURPOSE Identify eligible new orders and vehicle assignments at a decision epoch.
INPUT visible new/pending orders, prior feasible plan, implementation time, model
OUTPUT assignment eligibility and explicit optional screening scope
REFERENCES OrderManager.Generating_Ordr_Assgnmnt_Constr; periodic order assignment

PROCEDURE ScreenNewOrders(newOrders,priorPlan,ImT,newModel)
    state := SnapshotCommittedState(priorPlan,ImT)
    FOR each visible uncommitted order r
        candidates := empty set
        FOR each physical vehicle k
            start := state.residualSources[k]
            earliestReach := start.releaseTime + admissible travel-time lower bound
                from start.position to an allowed pickup/transfer entry for r
            modeAllowed := k's zone/type/schedule permits that service fragment
            deadlinePossible := earliestReach <= the relevant latest service time
            onwardPossible := an admissible lower bound permits remaining delivery
            IF modeAllowed AND deadlinePossible AND onwardPossible
                add k to candidates
            ELSE
                prohibit that k/r service assignment in newModel
        IF candidates is empty and no legal multimodal chain can serve r
            allow only r's unserved choice; record reason=unreachable
        ELSE
            preserve all candidate assignments for the coupled routing solve
        IF newModel.configuration.enableNeighborhoodHeuristic
            screen candidates using the declared route-distance/time neighborhood
            record excluded assignments and scope=screened_search
            never apply the screen to accepted unfinished service obligations
    return newModel with eligibility records and scope

PROCEDURE CheckOrderVisibility(order,decisionTime)
    REQUIRE order.submittedAt <= decisionTime
    return visible

ASSUMPTIONS
    Residual positions include the destination and release time of ongoing travel.
    Reachability bounds allow permitted transfer chains: one vehicle need not
    serve an order end-to-end. Default screening excludes assignments only when
    a necessary condition fails. Optional neighborhood screening restricts the
    search and is recorded as screened_search.
